    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d820">

                <pb facs="0818" n="714" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg714"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6183.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-16T19:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 16, 1913—7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President of Mexico has sent telegrams to the governors of all the Mexican
                    States announcing military intervention. Mr. Lascurain, from whom I received
                    this information, characterizes this course as “very dangerous.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
